$ SPC1 with an ID list that mixes a THRU range with single IDs, on the parent line and a continuation:
$ "1 THRU 2, 5" and then "7". Grids 1, 2, 5 and 7 are held in all six components; grids 5 and 7 must not move.
$ A reader that takes only "ID1 THRU ID2" drops 5 and 7, and the beam then moves there.
SOL 101
CEND
TITLE = SPC1 MIXED THRU LIST
SPC = 1
LOAD = 1
DISP = ALL
SPCFORCE = ALL
BEGIN BULK
GRID,1,,0.,0.,0.
GRID,2,,1.,0.,0.
GRID,3,,2.,0.,0.
GRID,4,,3.,0.,0.
GRID,5,,4.,0.,0.
GRID,6,,5.,0.,0.
GRID,7,,6.,0.,0.
CBAR,1,1,1,2,0.,1.,0.
CBAR,2,1,2,3,0.,1.,0.
CBAR,3,1,3,4,0.,1.,0.
CBAR,4,1,4,5,0.,1.,0.
CBAR,5,1,5,6,0.,1.,0.
CBAR,6,1,6,7,0.,1.,0.
PBAR,1,1,1.,0.1,0.1,0.2
MAT1,1,1.E7,,0.3
SPC1,1,123456,1,THRU,2,5,,,+S1
+S1,7
FORCE,1,4,,100.,0.,0.,1.
FORCE,1,6,,100.,0.,0.,1.
ENDDATA
